    {
      "actual_eos_at_stop": true,
      "answer_segment": "To determine the selling price of each watermelon, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Calculate the total cost of the watermelons:**\n   The vendor bought 50 watermelons for $80. Therefore, the total cost is:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total cost} = \\$80\n   \\]\n\n2. **Determine the selling price per watermelon:**\n   The vendor sold all the watermelons at a profit of 25%. First, we need to find the profit amount. The profit is 25% of the total cost:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Profit} = 0.25 \\times \\text{Total cost} = 0.25 \\times 80 = \\$20\n   \\]\n\n   Now, add the profit to the total cost to find the selling price:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Selling price} = \\text{Total cost} + \\text{Profit} = 80 + 20 = \\$100\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the selling price per watermelon:**\n   Since the vendor sold all 50 watermelons at the selling price of $100, the selling price per watermelon is:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Selling price per watermelon} = \\frac{\\text{Selling price}}{\\text{Number of watermelons}} = \\frac{100}{50} = \\$2\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the selling price of each watermelon is \\(\\boxed{2}\\).",
      "boundary_offset": null,
      "retained_tokens": 333,
      "stop_reason": "native_eos",
      "trigger_text": null
    },
    {
      "actual_eos_at_stop": true,
      "answer_segment": "To determine how old John's youngest son will be in 3 years, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Determine James's current age:**\n   - James is currently twice as old as his sister Dora.\n   - Dora will turn 12 in 3 years.\n   - Therefore, Dora's current age is \\(12 - 3 = 9\\) years old.\n   - Since James is twice as old as Dora, James's current age is \\(2 \\times 9 = 18\\) years old.\n\n2. **Determine John's current age:**\n   - John had a son James when he was 19 years old.\n   - Therefore, John's current age is \\(19 + 18 = 37\\) years old.\n\n3. **Determine the age of John's youngest son:**\n   - John's youngest son was born when John was 32 years old.\n   - Therefore, John's youngest son is currently \\(37 - 32 = 5\\) years old.\n\n4. **Determine the age of John's youngest son in 3 years:**\n   - John's youngest son is currently 5 years old.\n   - In 3 years, John's youngest son will be \\(5 + 3 = 8\\) years old.\n\nThus, John's youngest son will be \\(\\boxed{8}\\) years old in 3 years.",
