    {
      "actual_eos_at_stop": true,
      "answer_segment": "To determine the total cost Mark paid for the new radiator and the installation, we need to break down the problem into smaller steps and calculate each part separately.\n\n1. **Calculate the discount on the radiator:**\n   The original cost of the radiator is $400, and Mark gets it at 80% off. To find the discount amount, we multiply the original cost by the discount percentage:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Discount amount} = 400 \\times 0.80 = 320\n   \\]\n   So, the cost of the radiator after the discount is:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Cost after discount} = 400 - 320 = 80\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the cost of hiring the mechanic:**\n   The mechanic charges $50 per hour and it takes 3 hours to install the radiator. Therefore, the cost of hiring the mechanic is:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Cost of hiring the mechanic} = 50 \\times 3 = 150\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the total cost:**\n   The total cost is the sum of the cost of the radiator after the discount and the cost of hiring the mechanic:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total cost} = 80 + 150 = 230\n   \\]\n\nThus, the total amount Mark paid is \\(\\boxed{230}\\).",
